aining programs, including student paid electives at its campuses; and manufacturer or dealer sponsored training at various campuses and dedicated training centers. The company serves students, partners, and communities by providing education and support services in various fields. Universal Technical Institute, Inc. was founded in 1965 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerome A. Grant | CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Universal Technical Institute I is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $946M market cap on $836M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.027699227934846016},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot RO